 ## 1. The workflow — `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
 
-One file, four jobs (chained with `needs:`):
+Runs on every pull request and every push to `master` and `claude/**` (the branches the HQ agents prepare), except docs-only changes (`paths-ignore`: `specs/`, `docs/`, `CLAUDE.md`, READMEs, `plans/`, `reports/`). On branches a newer push cancels the older run; on `master` runs queue.
 
-| Job | Trigger | What it does |
+| Job (check name) | When | What it does |
 |---|---|---|
-| `test` | every PR + push to master | Type-checks API + Web, runs the full Vitest unit suite (~260 tests, 3 s) |
-| `smoke` | every PR + push to master, after `test` | Boots a Postgres 15 service container, pushes the Drizzle schema, starts the API in the background, registers a throwaway user, then runs every `*.smoke.ts` file with the resulting `SMOKE_USER_TOKEN` |
-| `e2e` | every PR + push to master, after `test` | Same Postgres container + boots the API + boots Next dev on :3001, then runs Playwright (Chromium, mobile-only, 5 golden flows). Uploads the HTML report as an artifact on failure |
-| `post-deploy-smoke` | push to master only, after `test` + `smoke` + `e2e` | Polls Railway until the new build is live (up to 5 min), asserts the API auth middleware, login route, and web landing/login pages return the expected HTTP code |
+| `test` (`Lint + tests`) | always | Schema drift check (`schema.ts` vs the committed migrations), type-checks API + Web, runs the API Vitest suite (some 400 test files, a few minutes) |
+| `smoke` (`Route smoke (Postgres + API)`) | after `test` | Postgres 15 service container, applies the real migrations (`db:migrate`, the same production runs on deploy) and the seed, boots the API, registers a throwaway user and runs every `*.smoke.ts` with its token; fails if a smoke test skipped unexpectedly |
+| `e2e-shard` (`E2E (Playwright) N/6`) | after `test` | Six shards, each with its own Postgres (migrations + seed), API and web, run the Playwright specs (Chromium, mobile; around 190 spec files) with `--shard=N/6`. The report is uploaded as an artifact |
+| `e2e` (`E2E (Playwright)`) | after the shards | One check, green only when every shard passed |
+| `post-deploy-smoke` (`Production smoke`) | push to `master` only | `scripts/smoke-remote.sh` against production: read-only liveness checks (the API, the auth gate, the web pages). Nothing deploys on push, so it is a canary, not proof that this commit is live |
 
-If `post-deploy-smoke` fails, the workflow turns red — Railway has already deployed but at least the team is notified.
+Failures come out as annotations (file, line and message), which the HQ office reads without a token.
 
